From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yevhen Salitrynskyi <ysalitrynskyi@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 21:26:54 -0500
Subject: feat: a link closed in a little window is a row of the archive
 (S-159)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

A little window closed by hand already went on the recently-closed list
(docs/features/little.md E13), and the archive listed its link as "in a
closed window of 1 tabs" with no Space. Its row now says "from a little
window", the Space filter offers "Little windows" while such a row is
listed, and the command bar's archived row says "Archived · Little
window" (docs/features/archive.md A17). A closed window or group of one
tab no longer says "of 1 tabs", and Forget on a little window's row is
plain Forget.

Why: Arc keeps links closed from Little Arc in its archive, with a
filter for them (Arc's 2023 release notes).
Removable when: never; Stedding's own archive.
